WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.200
The distance between points 'A' and 'B' is 8 kilometers.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:13.020
Zen begins at point 'A' and covers half this distance at 2 kilometers per hour.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.080
Half the distance would be 4 kilometers.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.640
and from this point to B,

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.280
he travels at 4 kilometers per hour.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.260
As the total distance is 8 kilometers,

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:27.860
and this is 4 kilometers, this distance will equal 4 kilometers.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.340
So he runs half the distance at 2 kilometers per hour.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.660
And the remaining half at 4 kilometers per hour.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.020
What will be his average speed?

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.240
Yes, we haven't seen this concept of average speed earlier!

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.720
Pause the video and try to find this average speed.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:51.520
It's easy.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.920
As he travels half the distance at 2 kilometres per hour,

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.900
and the remaining half at 4 kilometres per hour,

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:01.700
his average speed will be 2 plus 4 over 2.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.020
This is the average of the two numbers.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.040
That will be 6 over 2 or 3 kilometres per hour.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.400
That's Zen's average speed over this distance.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:13.660
And as some of you might have guessed.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.900
This is a classic mistake that many students make.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.420
So what is the average speed?

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:23.340
There is just one thing we need to understand about average speed.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.580
It equals the ratio of the total distance travelled

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.780
to the total time taken to travel that distance.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.600
Yes, total distance divided by the total time.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.740
So let's see what it will be in this case.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:41.300
The total distance travelled is '4 plus 4' or '8 kilometers'.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.860
And what is the total time taken?

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.300
We haven't been given the total time taken.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.180
But can we find that out?

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.400
The time taken is equal to the distance divided by the speed.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.380
And the total time taken will equal the sum of the

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.800
times taken to travel each part.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:02.920
The time taken to travel the initial '4 kilometres' will equal '4 over 2'.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.520
And the time taken to travel the second part will equal 4 over 4.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.280
The sum equals the total time taken by Zen

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.340
to cover the distance between points 'A' and 'B'.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.660
The numerator will equal 8.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.740
And the denominator will equal 'two plus 1'.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:22.940
Zen takes 3 hours to travel from point 'A to point B'.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:26.200
We get the average speed as '8 over 3'.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:30.040
That's approximately 2.66 km per hour.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.640
Wait a moment.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.080
Look at the two speeds Zen travelled at.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.640
Two and four kilometres per hour.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.220
Why is the average speed closer to two?

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.860
Why isn't it closer to four?

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:46.400
Here's the answer! The average speed is closer to two kilometres per hour

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.800
because Zen is travelling for more time at that speed.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.680
He is travelling at two kilometres per hour for two hours.

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:56.820
And at four kilometres per hour for one hour.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.080
If Zen would have travelled for more time

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.060
at four kilometres per hour,

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:04.420
the average speed would have been closer to four kilometres per hour

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.320
and not two kilometers per hour.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.380
Now let's look at a new example on a new page.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:15.540
Zen travels at two kilometers per hour for half hour.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:18.860
And then at four kilometers per hour for two hours.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.580
What will be his average speed?

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.840
Pause the video and give it a shot.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.920
We just learnt that the average speed equals the total distance

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.620
divided by the total time taken to travel that distance.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:41.180
Do we have the total distance? No, but we can find that out.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:44.180
Yes, it will be the sum of these two distances.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.480
The product of speed and time gives us the distance.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:51.220
Two multiplied by one half will give us this distance.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.160
And four times two will give us this distance.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.320
This sum gives us the total distance.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:01.440
And the total time will equal the sum of these two time duration's.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.260
One half plus two.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.760
This is one plus eight which is nine.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.720
And the denominator will be 0.5 plus 2 which is 2.5.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.540
Let's zoom out and write the answer.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.120
We get 9 over 2.5.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.720
To solve this we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by 4.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:25.500
We get 36 over 10 which equals 3.6  kilometres per hour.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.560
This as we can see is closer to four kilometres per hour.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.160
It's closer to 4 kilometers per hour

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.600
because he's travelling for more time at that speed.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:40.260
Let's look at one last problem to understand average speed.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.780
Zen travels at 3 kilometers per hour for 6 kilometers.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.040
And 5 kilometers per hour for 10 kilometers.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:50.480
What will be his average speed?

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.780
Pause the video and solve this one.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.840
The average speed is the ratio of the total distance,

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:05.060
to the total time taken to travel that distance.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.080
The total distance will be 6 plus 10.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:10.140
What will be the total time?

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:14.220
It will be the sum of the time duration's for each of these parts.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.940
The time taken to cover this part will equal 6 over 3 or 2 hours.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:24.260
And the time taken to travel this part will equal '10 over 5' or 2 hours.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:28.700
So the total time will equal 2 plus 2 or 4 hours.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.560
That will equal 16 over 4.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.680
4 kilometres per hour.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.500
Is this closer to 3 or to 5?

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.800
It's equidistant from each.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.160
And why is that?

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.360
It's because he is traveling for the same time at each of the speeds.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:47.840
Hence this is the average of the individual speed rates.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.380
We will look at more examples of average speed

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.380
over the next few sessions.

